{"id": "EUVD-2026-77165", "enisaUuid": "83457e2d-c39b-3fb3-be65-7696b5ca63bb", "description": "A vulnerability was found in GPAC up to f1219cde. This affects the function gf_svg_attributes_copy of the file scenegraph/svg_attributes.c of the component MP4Box. Performing a manipulation results in buffer over-read. The attack is only possible with local access. The exploit has been made public and could be used. Upgrading to version abi-16.23 mitigates this issue. The patch is named afca1f1181668d85941d51ed1adf647807d5d975. Upgrading the affected component is recommended.", "datePublished": "2026-09-14T00:45:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-15T13:58:39", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P", "references": ["https://vuldb.com/vuln/403192", "https://vuldb.com/vuln/403192/cti", "https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-90610", "https://vuldb.com/submit/913516", "https://github.com/gpac/gpac/issues/3819", "https://github.com/r1ck9-2q/cve_summit/blob/main/Vuln%20GPAC%20MP4Box%20Heap-Buffer-Overflow%20READ%20size%2020%20in%20gf_svg_attributes_copy.md", "https://github.com/gpac/gpac/commit/afca1f1181668d85941d51ed1adf647807d5d975", "https://github.com/gpac/gpac/releases/tag/abi-16.23", "https://github.com/gpac/gpac/"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6458-gwqx-h3fr", "CVE-2026-90610"], "assigner": "VulDB", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "bede0f43-09e6-39b1-b3f9-b6f3ea187dad", "product": {"name": "GPAC", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "f1219cde"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0e447548-0760-3736-91fd-5d0b102399c8", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}], "isExploited": false}